; expect 11
; A trait OTHER than `Show` claiming the name `show`, with an instance
; for `Int` only. The written instance still wins where it exists; its
; absence reaches the builtin for every other type - including the two
; the builtin SPLICES (a `String` stands in for the call, a `Bool`
; becomes the two-literal `if`), which is the shape that pins
; `traitRewrite`'s contract with `checkExprH`: the builtin's answer is
; passed up, so a spliced node is re-checked as what it now is.
; Measured before that was so: `AX3004 expected function type, found
; ()` at the `String` call, where AX3025 had been before the builtin.
;
;   "true"       4   spliced, under a trait with no `Bool` instance
;   "{x = 1}"    7   derived, under a trait with no `P` instance
;                11
(import Str)

(import Fmt)

(trait (Render a) where
  (show :: (-> a String)))

(impl (Render Int) where
  ((show (lambda (n) (fmtInt n)))))

(struct P
  (x : Int))

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (+ (strLen (show true)) (strLen (show (P 1)))))
